      "writtenOn": "2020-09-15T16:15:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Modification isn\u0027t the issue since it\u0027s passed by value then. This makes it a bit easier to recurse and avoid pass-by-value there - see the Addr() call on line 72 (in PS2). (Note that Addr() only works on structs and fields in structs when the structs are addressable, which they aren\u0027t when passed by value on the stack.)\n\nIt\u0027s of course possible to convert the value to a pointer here, but I think this is better since it\u0027s very likely a mistake.",
      "parentUuid": "22a521c0_bf9cbc62",
      "revId": "e5bf895264f4551430e9e33b4d738d80d75559ff",
